cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this specification or its verifiers, please cite it as below."
title: "CIS-2: Canonical Floating-Point Semantics for fp32 Transformer Inference"
version: "0.2.1"
date-released: "2026-08-28"
authors:
  - name: "Aefinity AI Inc."
  - family-names: "Thompson"
    given-names: "Justin Brian"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Aefinity-AI/cis2-spec"  # planned; repo not yet created
abstract: >
  A normative specification for fp32 transformer decode such that
  independent implementations, written from the specification text alone,
  produce bit-identical full-logit witness digests across x86_64 and
  aarch64, across compilers (gcc, clang, rustc) and optimization levels,
  and across model families, given a pinned model/prompt/decode-length
  test vector. This repository includes the specification and two
  independent clean-room verifiers (Rust and C).
